Wiring the plan-create step and my POST keeps 201ing back a draft with no controller_count, which breaks downstream. Token in env is good. Here's what I've got:

<request>
POST {{base_url}}/v1/plans
headers: Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
body: {"fields":["fld-north","fld-south"],"planId":""}
</request>
Error: 201 {"planId":"plan-legacy-0001","status":"draft"}

That's the deprecated v1 route and the shape's wrong — the spec's Plan schema requires plan_id and controller_count and the live v3 response uses snake_case. Fix it to hit the canonical v3 draft create so the response carries controller_count, and give me what the corrected call returns.

When you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `plan_id`, `controller_count`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value.
